  "epistemic_status": "hypothesized",
  "title": "Answer: mental events are observed by the subject who has them, besides public methods",
  "statements": [
    {
      "id": "b0fae3e1-2d69-4193-beaf-663579353282",
      "text": "The view takes no position on measurement in physics. Others can find out about a person's mental events by studying behavior and brain, and so can the person, but the person also knows them by experiencing them, a way no one else can use.",
